  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}+1).$ Calculate the velocity at time $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The velocity is the derivative of the position function $x(t)$ with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({t}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
